// What a type looks like, written down once.
//
// Four libraries in this family each keep their own idea of a field —
// moonapi for request bodies and OpenAPI, moonorm for columns, moongql for
// SDL, moonschema for validation — so a user model that must be checked,
// documented, stored and served is written four times today.
//
// This package is the description and nothing else: no reading, no writing,
// no dependencies. The projections are subpackages, so a program that wants
// OpenAPI does not link the SQL writer.
//
// What this is not: MoonBit already has derive(ToJson) and derive(FromJson),
// and core's @json carries JsonPath and JsonDecodeError. Converting a struct
// to JSON is not missing and is not re-done here. A description says what a
// type looks like; decoding stays the language's job.
